From 03716ad101ab0e135420aa88b61a1a3166e82a99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:03:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][VideoPlayer] Upscalers: AiUpscale Fast, for film and
 for animation

Two more choices of the three upscaler settings (expert, off by default):
AiUpscale Fast 2x with its Photo model ("AiUpscale (film)") and with its
LineArt model ("AiUpscale (animation)"), mpv user shaders of
Alexkral/AviSynthAiUpscale at d04cf8154e4b (2021-03-28, the head of master),
kept byte for byte in system/hades/upscalers with their SHA256 in SOURCES.md.

Measured as the upscalers of 1.1 were (libplacebo of the build on Mesa's
software GLES 3.1; pictures made half their size with Catmull-Rom and drawn
back, against the original), on three anime frames, six film frames in SDR
and in PQ, and pictures of subtitles, lines and outlines; against Lanczos 3:
- animation: +1.06 to +1.09 dB of PSNR of the luma (FSRCNNX 16 +0.94), SSIM
  +0.0020 (+0.0017);
- film, SDR: +3.90 to +4.09 dB (+3.75), SSIM +0.0029 to +0.0034 (+0.0017);
- film, PQ: +3.31 to +3.44 dB (+3.86), SSIM +0.0014 to +0.0019 (+0.0010),
  Delta E ITP 1.53 to 1.58 on average (1.59), the same 99th percentile;
- about 20 times the GPU work of Lanczos 3 (FSRCNNX 16 about 28);
- more overshoot at hard edges than FSRCNNX 16 (film in SDR: 0.29 against
  0.14 thousandths of the signal on average), about that of FSRCNNX 8.
So it sits between FSRCNNX 8 and 16 in cost, nearer than FSRCNNX 16 on
animation and on SDR film, a little less near in PQ. The two models are the
same network with other weights; LineArt is made for drawn lines.

The files are GPL-3.0: their repository carries the text of the GNU GPL
version 3 and names no later version, so they are taken as GPL-3.0 only.
They are separate files that libplacebo reads when a video is drawn with
them; the Kodi of LibreELEC Hades is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later
(LICENSES/README.md), with which they are compatible.

Their shaders run where the picture is drawn more than 1.4 times its size
in width and height (their //!WHEN lines; UpscalerChoice.h ShadersRun()).
Everything else is that of the other upscalers: the automatic turn-off when
the GPU does not keep up, the log lines, the buttons of the player
information, and the settings' help in English and Spanish.
